<header><p class="enc-kicker">Event · other</p><h1 class="enc-title">Frog Lake massacre</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">2 April 1885</span></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Frog Lake massacre took place on 2 April 1885 at Frog Lake in present-day <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/alberta">Alberta</a>, during the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/north-west-rebellion">North-West Resistance</a>. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cree">Cree</a> warriors of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/big-bear">Big Bear</a>'s band, led by the war chief Wandering Spirit, killed nine people, including the Indian agent Thomas Quinn and two Catholic priests. Wandering Spirit was among the eight men hanged at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battleford">Battleford</a> later that year.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/frog-lake-massacre.jpg" alt="Frog Lake massacre" width="320" height="248" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Toronto Lithographing Co. · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:MURDER_OF_THE_PRIESTS_AT_FROG_LAKE.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
